  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the call to action text",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the textual material 'put an end to domestic abuse!' as the intended audience for the call to action. The text directly addresses the viewer, urging them to take societal action against domestic abuse, thereby positioning the user as the agent of change. This projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but is implied through the imperative nature of the message and the visual context of suffering, which demands viewer response.",
